{"name":"Ranch Mink","hex":"#968379","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ranch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large plot of land used for raising cattle, sheep or other livestock.","A small farm that cultivates vegetables or livestock, especially one in the Southwestern United States."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To operate a ranch; to engage in ranching.","To work on a ranch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ranch"},{"term":"mink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any semi-aquatic, carnivorous mammal in the Mustelinae subfamily, similar to weasels, with dark fur, native to Europe and America, of which two species in different genera are extant: the American mink (Neogale vison) and the European mink (Mustela lutreola).","The fur or pelt of a mink, used to make apparel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ranch","blocks":[{"text":"A ranch is an area of land, including various structures, given primarily to ranching, the practice of raising grazing livestock such as cattle and sheep. It is a subtype of farm. These terms are most often applied to livestock-raising operations in Mexico, the Western United States and Western Canada, though there are ranches in other areas. People who own or operate a ranch are called ranchers, cattlemen, or stockgrowers. Ranching is also a method used to raise less common livestock such as horses, elk, American bison, ostrich, emu, and alpaca."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg/330px-Grant-Kohrs_Ranch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranch","wikidata":"Q509028"},{"title":"Mink","blocks":[{"text":"Mink are dark-coloured, semiaquatic, carnivorous mammals in the genera Mustela and Neogale and part of the family Mustelidae, which also includes weasels, stoats, martens, otters, badgers, and others. There are two extant species referred to as \"mink\", the American mink and the European mink. The extinct sea mink was related to the American mink but was much larger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/American_Mink.jpg/330px-American_Mink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mink","wikidata":"Q17700"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/1280px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaler_der_Grabkammer_des_Sennudem_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Principales_vias_pecuarias.png/500px-Principales_vias_pecuarias.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Principales_vias_pecuarias.png/500px-Principales_vias_pecuarias.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Main transhumance routes in Spain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrincipales_vias_pecuarias.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Garrochista_Espa%C3%B1ol_-_Spanish_Shepherd.jpg/500px-Garrochista_Espa%C3%B1ol_-_Spanish_Shepherd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://th